exports[`lectio-gates run > runs a dummy gate end to end: exit code, log, JSON report and PR comment > comment.md 1`] = `
"<!-- lectio-gates -->
## Lectio gates: a gate failed

> Offline run: sources were checked with the offline fake fetcher, so every web source reads as missing (expect commentary-unchecked warnings). the content workflows run with the live fetcher.

| Gate | Status | Details |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Always passes (\`always-pass\`) | Pass | no findings |
| Dummy gate (\`dummy\`) | Fail | 2 errors, 1 warning, 1 note |

### Findings

#### Pull request

- **info** · \`dummy/file-count\` (Dummy gate): 2 passages changed
  - Rule: A content PR changes at most one passage.
  - Fix: Split the PR so each passage is reviewed on its own.

#### \`passages/MT.20.1-16.json\`

**Whole file**

- **warning** · \`dummy/summary-short\` (Dummy gate) at \`/summary\`: summary is 111 characters
  - Rule: A passage summary stays under 100 characters.
  - Fix: Shorten the summary to one plain sentence.

**Claim \`c2\`**

- **error** · \`dummy/claim-cites-source\` (Dummy gate) at \`/claims/1/sourceIds\`: claim c2 cites no source
  - Rule: Every claim cites at least one source.
  - Fix: Add the id of a supporting source to the claim’s sourceIds.

**Claim \`c10\`**

- **error** · \`dummy/claim-cites-source\` (Dummy gate) at \`/claims/2/sourceIds\`: claim c10 cites no source
  - Rule: Every claim cites at least one source.
  - Fix: Add the id of a supporting source to the claim’s sourceIds.

<sub>Base \`origin/main\` · head \`HEAD\` · 4 changed files. Each finding names its rule; the fix says what to change.</sub>
"
`;

